{"id": "110067", "revid": "195012", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=110067", "title": "Pabna", "text": "Pabna, in north-eastern Bangladesh, within the Rajshahi Division, is an interesting mix of Hindu temples, British-era palaces, natural wetlands and criss-crossing rivers, complete with century-old bridges. The capital of the district, also known as \"Pabna\", sits to the south, on the northern bank of the Padma River, and is home to most of the archaeological structures.\nGet in.\nBy train.\nYou can go to Pabna by train. It's very easy to go Pabna from Dhaka. First you have to go Komlapur rail station. You can buy a ticket from there for Dhaka to Pabna. \nBy bus.\nBus tickets from capital Dhaka via Aricha to Pabna costs Tk 300 to Tk 450."}
{"id": "110117", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=110117", "title": "Severn Valley Railway", "text": "The Severn Valley Railway is a steam heritage tourist line in England. It runs for 16 mi.\nGet in.\nThe Severn Valley Railway can be accessed from any of the stations on the railways route, although most visitors will start their trip at either end of the line.\nThe railway does not have direct interchanges with the rest of the UK rail network, although Kidderminster Town is a short walk from Kidderminster (SVR) station.\nBy car.\nIt is signposted from M5 Junctions 3 and 6 (northbound only), and locally in Kidderminster, Standard UK Brown tourist navigation signs are used.\nGet around.\nThe best method of travelling between locations is the railway itself, with most of the rail-related attractions being on or within walking distance of them.\nSingle tickets are available for \u00a35-14.50 one way for adults and seniors (\u00a33.50-10 for children), or \u00a38.50-21 return (\u00a35.50-14) (Dec 2018).\nFreedom of the Line tickets allow unlimited travel during the day between Kidderminster and Bridgnorth and free entry into the Engine House Visitor Centre at Highley (Dec 2018):\nDiscounts are available if booked five working days in advance either online or by telephone on +44 1562 757900. \nUpgrade to first class for \u00a34 one way or \u00a38 for the day. Multi-day passes are available.\nSee.\nThe railway also operates special events[dead link] across the railway, and at the Engine House.\nBuy.\nSome SVR stations have gift shops. Bridgnorth also has a well-stocked transport bookshop.\nEat.\nAn on train 'trolley' service is provided.\nThere is a refreshment facility at Bridgnorth, and an on-station pub (offering pub snacks).\nAlso a refreshment facility Kidderminster, and an on-station pub (King and Castle) with a good selection of real ales.\nFlag and Whistle Stop - in the Engine House (Highley).\nConnect.\nThe area through which the Severn Valley Railway passes is served by most UK phone operators, and all stations have access to the UK telephone system."}
{"id": "110121", "revid": "132185", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=110121", "title": "Lakeland (disambiguation)", "text": "There is more than one place called Lakeland:\nUnited States of America.\nLakeland is also the name of unincorporated locations in Louisiana (Wikipedia) &amp; Michigan (Wikipedia).\nSouth Lakeland.\nUnited Kingdom.\nSouth Lakeland is also commonly used to refer to the southern part of Lakeland, Florida; specifically, the large, populous region south of the central business district and north of Mulberry.\nNot to be confused with.\n\"See also: Lake District.\""}
{"id": "110122", "revid": "1423298", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=110122", "title": "Woqooyi Galbeed", "text": "Woqooyi Galbeed, sometimes known as \"Maroodi Jeex\", is one of the administrative regions of Somaliland. Containing Somaliland's capital and two largest cities, it forms the most populous and important region in the country. It also houses the largest number of attractions and sights when compared to the rest of Somaliland.\nGet in.\nThere is a major international airport in \"Hargeisa\" which connects the region to numerous other countries.\nSee.\nLaas Geel, which is about 60 km from Hargeisa, is one of the best examples, if not \"the\" best example, of prehistoric cave art on the African continent.\nStay safe.\nWhen venturing outside of the capital, Hargeisa, it is compulsory to take a government security guard with you, called a \"SPU\". It is possible to apply for an exemption, but is a time-consuming process."}
{"id": "110138", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=110138", "title": "Xiamen/Haicang", "text": "Haicang (\u6d77\u6ca7; \"H\u00e1i-chhng\" in Minnan, \"H\u01ceic\u0101ng\" in Mandarin) is a suburb of Xiamen.\nUnderstand.\nAdministratively, Haicang is part of Xiamen City but geographically, it is distinct. It is west of downtown on the mainland, connected to Xiamen Island by a bridge. There is a map in the Xiamen article. However, unlike some other mainland suburbs, Haicang is not yet on the Xiamen BRT (bus rapid transit) system.\nIt the last few years, Haicang has been growing quickly. There are many new buildings, many of them highrise and some quite luxurious.\nGet in.\nThe usual route to get from Xiamen Island to Haicang is to cross the Haicang Bridge.\nBy metro.\nHaicang can be reached via Line 2 of the Xiamen Metro. It connects Wuyuanwan in Xiamen Island to Tianzhushan in Haicang District with 32 stations on the route. It operates from 5:40 to 22:00 with tickets ranging from RMB 2 to 7.\nBy bus.\nBuses from the South, e.g. from Guangdong or Zhangzhou, often have a stop in Haicang en route to Xiamen.\nBy boat.\nThe main ferry terminal is at Songyu Wharf (\u5d69\u5c7f\u7801\u5934). Ferries depart from Xiamen Wharf No. 1 (\u53a6\u95e8\u7b2c\u4e00\u7801\u5934) on the west coast of Xiamen Island.\nGet around.\nThere are taxis, ride hailing apps and buses.\nGo next.\nHaicang is on the main highway between Xiamen and Zhangzhou, so either of those is an obvious next stop. "}
