{"id": "110832", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=110832", "title": "Lewistown (Montana)", "text": "Called \"The Heart of Montana\", Lewistown has many of the activities that make Montana a tourist destination, from big game and bird hunting to fishing, camping, biking, hiking and skiing. It is the geographic center of the state. The population was 5,901 at the 2010 census.\nUnderstand.\nIt is surrounded by five mountain ranges: the Snowies, the Judiths, the Moccasins, the Belts, and the Highwoods.\nBe sure to pronounce the town correctly - Lewis-\"town\" not Lewis-\"ton\" - or the locals will let you know your mistake.\nGet in.\nLewistown is on U.S. Highway 87 (US-87) and Montana Highway 200 (MT-200) from the east and west. From the north it is on U.S. Highway 191 (US-191).\nGet around.\nAs with most of Montana, a vehicle is the best way to get around. The historic downtown area is walkable, and walking tour maps can be picked up at the Chamber.\nWhen adventuring outside of town, be sure you plan for fuel and download maps. Wide open country is great to explore, just don't expect to always have service and amenities."}
