{"id": "110846", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=110846", "title": "Sidney (Montana)", "text": "Sidney is a town in Montana. In 2020, 6,300 people lived there.\nUnderstand.\nThe area is near large oil reserves and has experienced several boom and bust cycles. These bring in an influx of people to the town, some staying for a short period of time. The town has surges in oil exploration activity. The entire region has had substantial increase in population. This has brought a tremendous increase in the economy, the population and crime.\nSidney is home to a sugar beet refinery. In the fall the refining creates a lingering odor over the entire town. It's not exactly unpleasant, just odd smelling.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nSidney is at the intersection of State Highway 200 (MT-200) and State Highway 16 (MT-16). It can also be accessed by MT-23.\nGet around.\nThere is a standard downtown area with businesses in a walkable area. Several businesses, restaurants, and most hotels, are outside this area.\nSleep.\nMany workers stay in hotels and campgrounds. Reservations are critical."}
